WEBVTT

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:16.900
When I have 1000 or lower LP, I get one 
random Link Monster in the Data Storm!

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.970
Storm Access is a powerful move using the 
data material that creates the Data Storm.

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.710
A normal duelist can't use this Skill.

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:39.080
Can Playmaker do this because he has a 
special connection with data material?

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.700
Why does he have a connection?

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:45.200
Ten years ago...  Three things...

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.160
You're the one from that 
incident ten years ago?

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:54.270
That's right.  I'm that emissary of revenge!

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.500
Incident ten years ago?

00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:02.500
Is it related to the incident ten 
years ago that they discussed?

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:06.820
Since SOL Technologies created LINK VRAINS...

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:10.620
...I should find something 
by searching their data bank.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:18.960
A cyber treasure hunter like me can create 
a backdoor program to access the data bank.

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.170
Almost there...  I'm close 
to accessing the data bank...

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.110
I did it!

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:40.080
Data Storm?

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:42.810
Just when I'm close to 
accessing the data bank!

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:49.150
If I don't get past this...

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:06.060
No good.  I couldn't access it.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.940
But I won't give up.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:14.360
As a cyber treasure hunter, 
Playmaker ignites my curiosity.

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:32.700
I run Across the universe

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:35.870
At the speed of light

00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.740
Begin Loading

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:41.470
Open the door of dreams

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:45.040
VRAINS spreads

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.150
Believe in myself

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:51.680
VRAINS continues

00:02:51.930 --> 00:02:56.990
The circuit draws the future

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:01.060
I'll grab it with my own hands  Yeah

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.660
Access!

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.360
Start swirling, Data Storm!

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:06.970
I'm now With the Wind

00:03:07.150 --> 00:03:09.270
Link with my soul

00:03:09.380 --> 00:03:12.040
Speed up, Data Storm!

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:13.770
Now Win the Race

00:03:13.890 --> 00:03:16.610
Connected world

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:20.110
No matter when

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.480
Nothing is impossible

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:27.620
Strive for hope

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:32.190
And ride the wind!

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:01.720
Ch-Chief Zaizen, here you go!

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.560
Thank you.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:05.720
Hot!

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:08.880
I'm sorry!

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:11.070
It's fine.

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:15.520
Hayami, how long have you 
been with the company?

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.360
You want to know my private info?

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:20.800
Are you attracted to me?

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:24.280
I want to know my worker's 
history - as your boss.

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.690
I'm sorry that I misunderstood!

00:04:28.690 --> 00:04:32.280
Umm...  It'll be three years since I joined!

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:37.820
That means you don't know the location of 
the data of the incident ten years ago.

00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:42.990
Correct.  My duty is to 
manage equipment, not data.

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.230
All SOL Technologies data 
is stored in this room.

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:52.720
It's right before my eyes, but 
I can't lay a finger on it.

00:04:55.890 --> 00:04:58.320
Excuse me.  I'm leaving.

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:00.620
Let them know I'm going home.

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.990
U-Understood!

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:09.650
Zaizen was demoted to Chief, 
but he's still cool!

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.630
SOL Technologies is heartless.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:19.730
Even though you protected LINK 
VRAINS, you were still demoted.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:25.430
Playmaker gave me Revolver's removal program.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:29.710
That's how Aoi regained consciousness.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:33.020
Even though I was demoted, I have no regrets.

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:37.950
Your replacement is Kitamura, 
your former boss.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:43.520
I believe he created a 
duelist army that used AI.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:48.040
What are you doing?

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.400
Do you know how behind this project is?

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:56.370
If you get any further behind, 
I'll cut your salary by 50%!

00:05:56.580 --> 00:05:59.600
We must protect LINK VRAINS from hackers!

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:04.940
I'll create an AI duelist 
army and crush the hackers!

00:06:05.490 --> 00:06:09.910
He'll do anything to deliver a result.

00:06:11.340 --> 00:06:14.570
SOL Technologies is full of scoundrels.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:18.660
But you can say that about 
any fast-growing company.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:26.020
Anyway, do you know what Playmaker 
meant about the incident ten years ago?

00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:28.310
Of course I don't.

00:06:28.310 --> 00:06:32.270
If I can't rely on you, I'll 
have to search on my own.

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:37.510
By using a backdoor program to infiltrate 
SOL Technologies' data bank.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:38.640
What?

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:43.200
Why do you think I take 
SOL Technologies' jobs?

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:48.120
The more connections I make, 
the more I can acquire.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:50.920
Will you give it to me?

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.800
Why do I have to give it to you?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:57.130
Or will you buy it at my asking price?

00:07:00.820 --> 00:07:05.200
I have no interest in men 
with no power or money.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.110
What are you going to do?

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.450
Maybe Playmaker will buy it.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:17.450
Because he's interested in 
the incident ten years ago.

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:20.930
See you.

00:07:28.900 --> 00:07:34.430
Someone guided me during 
Playmaker and Revolver's duel.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:41.280
Someone is guiding me?

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.710
I copied the source code, just in case.

00:07:45.710 --> 00:07:48.180
If I use it to make a program...

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:52.650
...the person watching over 
Playmaker will notice.

00:07:58.090 --> 00:08:00.220
No no.

00:08:00.220 --> 00:08:02.600
More to the right!

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:05.990
You're too loud.  Someone will notice.

00:08:05.990 --> 00:08:10.660
It's fine.  He's been in 
a daze since he came home.

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:14.670
No way!  A program can't have free will!

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:20.900
I naturally expected that reaction.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:27.150
But it doesn't matter if you 
believe this story or not.

00:08:27.640 --> 00:08:32.720
Ignis created the Cyberse and is 
trying to conquer the network.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:38.100
We'll do whatever it takes to 
kill Ignis and the Cyberse!

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.820
What did he mean?

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:44.200
I don't know.  I don't 
have enough information.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:49.380
It's me.  Can you come right now?

00:08:49.380 --> 00:08:51.040
Yeah.  What's up?

00:08:51.050 --> 00:08:54.050
Ooh, right there.  So nice!

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:55.130
You're too loud.

00:08:55.130 --> 00:08:56.820
Go back go back go back!

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:01.910
Are you going somewhere?

00:09:01.910 --> 00:09:05.090
Kusanagi wants to meet ASAP.  Let's go.

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:07.430
What?  I have a bad feeling about this.

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:15.080
Look at this.

00:09:17.310 --> 00:09:18.920
From Ghost Girl?

00:09:18.920 --> 00:09:22.990
She sent a message on a 
popular hacking forum.

00:09:22.990 --> 00:09:25.600
You two know each other?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.820
No, but I guided her during 
your duel against Revolver.

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:36.220
She acquired my source code to 
created a program that I'd notice.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.490
I see.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:41.860
She's demanding to duel Playmaker.

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.970
If she wins, she gets Playmaker's AI.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:47.230
What?  You must be kidding!

00:09:47.680 --> 00:09:51.970
Playmaker, you won't do 
something that dangerous.

00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:53.240
I accept.

00:09:53.240 --> 00:09:55.660
It says what she's offering in exchange.

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:59.790
The backdoor to SOL Technologies' data bank.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:00.710
What?

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:03.240
There's really a backdoor?

00:10:03.240 --> 00:10:05.090
That's what it says.

00:10:05.090 --> 00:10:07.100
It's a lie.

00:10:07.100 --> 00:10:10.120
No.  Her hacking skills are first class.

00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:13.680
She sent a portion of the 
data, and it looks real.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:18.860
Reply to Ghost Girl that I'll duel her.

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.020
Okay.

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:27.440
Where in the city are you, Playmaker?

00:10:31.020 --> 00:10:32.180
He answered.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.650
Into the VRAINS!

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:46.330
She's here!

00:10:46.330 --> 00:10:47.590
Ghost Girl?

00:10:47.590 --> 00:10:49.530
Yeah.  It's definitely her.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:51.700
You're really going to duel her?

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:54.410
She might have set a trap again.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:58.000
Yeah, I'm fully aware of that.  However...

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:04.980
#1: In her message, I sense Ghost Girl's 
determination, despite her weaknesses.

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:11.350
#2: There must be secret information about 
Hanoi in SOL Technologies' data bank.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:16.440
#3: I'll learn the truth about 
the incident ten years ago.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:22.260
Deck set!  Into the VRAINS!

00:11:34.650 --> 00:11:37.120
Nothing's happening.

00:11:37.370 --> 00:11:40.600
Not a single person is here.

00:11:40.600 --> 00:11:42.320
I know that!

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:48.430
But if we don't get the exclusive scoop, 
we can't create the Playmaker TV special!

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:54.990
Yeah.  Because the data you 
bought with our bonuses is gone!

00:11:54.990 --> 00:12:01.220
If we don't fill in the gaps to create 
the Playmaker TV special, we'll be fired!

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:03.680
I don't want that!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.260
Yamamoto!  That's...

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.170
Don't say my real name!

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.320
Don't worry.  No one's here.

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:21.690
Anyway, look at that!

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:24.940
I smell an exclusive scoop!

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.620
If we get this footage...

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:28.660
We'll get our bonuses back!

00:12:33.540 --> 00:12:35.700
Look!  It's Playmaker!

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.320
Nice looking out, boss!

00:12:37.320 --> 00:12:39.350
Just as you expected!

00:12:39.350 --> 00:12:42.400
Everyone will flip!  After them!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:43.710
Aye aye, sir!

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.580
You're here.

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.180
Good.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.750
The wind is strong today.

00:12:54.980 --> 00:12:57.200
Fly better!

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.680
Over there!  Film it!

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:03.800
Sheesh!  You don't treat pigeons nicely!

00:13:08.300 --> 00:13:10.540
You've accepted my challenge?

00:13:10.540 --> 00:13:14.570
Yeah.  But you're not lying 
about the exchange, right?

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.640
Of course not.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:18.110
I have the data ready.

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:22.360
It's the backdoor to SOL 
Technologies' data bank.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:26.450
It should have data about 
the incident ten years ago.

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:28.990
Why do you want to duel me?

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:30.920
Why don't you go there yourself?

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:35.890
If I acquire your AI, I can sell it 
to SOL Technologies at a high price.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:42.870
To be honest, I became interested in 
you after seeing your recent duel.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.620
Only as a cyber treasure hunter, of course.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:49.240
I want to know more about you.

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:51.620
Cyber treasure hunter?

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:57.050
She's definitely trying to trick us!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:14:00.090
Why don't humans learn from experience?

00:14:00.090 --> 00:14:04.350
Because humans can feel things 
instead of learning them.

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:07.830
You're really going to do this...

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:19.240
Here we go!

00:14:19.610 --> 00:14:21.420
Speed Duel!

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:30.850
Acquire the backdoor, Yusaku.

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:39.690
I have no information about her, 
but she definitely studied you.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:41.210
Probably.

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:44.560
You're clearly falling into her trap.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:49.430
But it's worth it if I can acquire 
the data bank's backdoor program.

00:14:49.430 --> 00:14:51.320
I go first!

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:55.170
I summon Altergeist Marionetter from my hand!

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:07.340
When this card is summoned, I can select an 
Altergeist trap card in my deck and set it.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:10.720
Then I set another card.

00:15:10.720 --> 00:15:12.590
I end my turn.

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:15.780
She has two set cards on her field.

00:15:15.780 --> 00:15:17.330
What's her strategy?

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:19.030
My turn!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:20.530
I draw!

00:15:21.660 --> 00:15:23.630
I summon Cyberse Wizard!

00:15:30.420 --> 00:15:31.780
Here I go!

00:15:31.780 --> 00:15:34.080
What?  She has two set cards!

00:15:34.300 --> 00:15:38.320
If I was scared, I wouldn't 
have accepted this duel.

00:15:39.290 --> 00:15:41.720
He's not worried about my set cards?

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.790
He really is interesting.

00:15:43.790 --> 00:15:44.790
Battle!

00:15:44.790 --> 00:15:48.900
Cyberse Wizard, attack 
Altergeist Marionetter!

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.900
Illusion Spike!

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.730
I activate Altergeist Kunquery's 
effect from my hand!

00:15:54.730 --> 00:15:58.470
I can Special Summon it 
and negate your attack!

00:16:00.800 --> 00:16:01.640
What?

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:05.790
I thought she wanted to use a trap, but 
she used an effect from her hand instead.

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:12.710
When the Special Summoned 
Kunquery is on my field...

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:16.240
...I can negate one of your cards' effects.

00:16:16.860 --> 00:16:20.460
She already negated our attacks and effects.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.810
And strengthened her defense.

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:25.720
She's cunning!

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:27.330
I end my turn.

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:30.200
My turn!  I draw!

00:16:30.200 --> 00:16:32.000
I'm only getting started!

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:36.080
I summon a second Altergeist Marionetter!

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:43.760
Due to Marionetter's effect, I select one 
Altergeist trap card in my deck and set it!

00:16:43.980 --> 00:16:45.860
Another set card.

00:16:45.860 --> 00:16:48.550
Three monsters and three set cards.

00:16:48.550 --> 00:16:50.090
It's a solid formation.

00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:53.090
If this shocks you, you have much to learn.

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.950
Here's my next plan!

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.300
She's making her move!

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:04.270
Open before me!  The circuit that connects 
to the unknown parallel universe!

00:17:07.260 --> 00:17:10.210
What?  She can Link Summon?

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:12.680
Arrowheads confirmed!

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:17.240
The summoning conditions are at 
least two Altergeist monsters!

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:21.650
I set two Marionetters and 
Kunquery in the Link Markers!

00:17:24.280 --> 00:17:26.230
Circuit combine!

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:28.530
Link Summon!

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:33.720
Appear, Link 3 Altergeist Primebanshee!

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:40.400
I activate the trap card, 
Altergeist Materialization!

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:43.180
I Special Summon Marionetter 
from my graveyard!

00:17:47.010 --> 00:17:48.780
I'm not done.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:52.810
I activate the Continuous 
Trap, Altergeist Protocol!

00:17:53.970 --> 00:17:59.830
Then due to Altergeist Marionetter's effect, 
I send Altergeist Protocol to the graveyard.

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:03.510
Resurrect, Altergeist Marionetter!

00:18:06.460 --> 00:18:11.200
I tribute Marionetter to 
activate Primebanshee's effect!

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:17.780
Once during each of our turns, I Special 
Summon an Altergeist from my deck next to its Link.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.380
Appear!

00:18:19.600 --> 00:18:22.290
Altergeist Meluseek!

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:26.560
I set one card!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.290
Oh my.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:35.020
After using three monsters to Link Summon, 
she already Special Summoned two more monsters!

00:18:35.020 --> 00:18:37.260
Her transition skills are amazing!

00:18:42.160 --> 00:18:45.170
Playmaker is taken aback!

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:48.040
Yeah.  She's playing really well.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:50.220
She's not letting her guard down.

00:18:50.220 --> 00:18:52.280
Be careful, Yusaku.

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:55.870
My preparations are done.

00:18:58.970 --> 00:19:04.920
Even if Playmaker has a special connection 
with LINK VRAINS' data material...

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:10.460
...I'll have no problems if I drop his 
LP to 0 before he activates his Skill.

00:19:11.030 --> 00:19:13.630
I'll end you this turn!

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:22.640
She has three Altergeists on her field.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:26.850
Even if she destroys Cyberse 
Wizard and attacks us directly...

00:19:26.850 --> 00:19:29.140
...the max damage we'll take is 2400.

00:19:29.140 --> 00:19:32.560
Too bad!  You can't drop our LP to 0!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:34.720
She miscalculated.

00:19:35.040 --> 00:19:38.940
No duelist would make 
such a simple math error!

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:41.090
There could be!

00:19:41.520 --> 00:19:45.700
Why does everyone want this dumb AI?

00:19:45.700 --> 00:19:46.820
How dare you!

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:49.380
Don't get angry when she's telling the truth.

00:19:49.970 --> 00:19:51.400
Okay...

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:52.570
Wait, what?

00:19:52.570 --> 00:19:58.180
Marionetter has high ATK, but 
she tributed it for Meluseek.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.420
There must be a reason why.

00:20:00.840 --> 00:20:03.290
Good instincts, Playmaker.

00:20:03.290 --> 00:20:07.180
This card can attack you directly, 
even if you have monsters.

00:20:07.180 --> 00:20:09.920
That still won't drop our LP to 0!

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:13.530
Altergeist Meluseek attacks you directly!

00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:15.530
Ectoplaster!

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:22.970
That was only 500 damage!

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:25.440
Meluseek's additional effect!

00:20:25.680 --> 00:20:31.810
When it deals you battle damage, one card 
on your field goes to the graveyard!

00:20:32.020 --> 00:20:34.410
Bye bye, Cyberse Wizard.

00:20:34.410 --> 00:20:38.520
After a direct attack, you're 
sending a monster to the graveyard?

00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:48.560
This was why she brought out Meluseek.

00:20:48.800 --> 00:20:52.570
The remaining monsters 
have a total of 3700 ATK.

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:54.330
This is bad, Playmaker!

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.930
You're already in a pinch!

00:20:56.140 --> 00:20:59.800
As I promised, I'll end you this turn!

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:01.270
Battle!

00:21:01.800 --> 00:21:06.250
Altergeist Marionetter 
attacks Playmaker directly!

00:21:15.860 --> 00:21:18.760
Playmaker will finally lose a duel!

00:21:19.140 --> 00:21:23.190
Now we won't be fired, Yamamoto!

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:29.420
We've been pursing Playmaker ever since 
he arrived in LINK VRAINS as a hero.

00:21:29.420 --> 00:21:34.170
But should I be happily 
filming Playmaker's defeat?

00:21:34.620 --> 00:21:39.510
Ghost Girl, your plan will 
drop Playmaker's LP to 0.

00:21:39.760 --> 00:21:44.350
It feels great to defeat 
the popular Playmaker.

00:21:44.350 --> 00:21:48.820
I'll acquire and sell that AI to 
SOL Technologies at a high price.

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:51.420
My dreams get larger!

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:54.290
It's over.  Prepare yourself!

00:21:54.290 --> 00:21:56.890
Don't lose, Playmaker!

00:21:56.890 --> 00:21:59.920
My fate is at stake!

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:26.850
Dance!  Strike with your heels

00:22:27.110 --> 00:22:30.390
Scream!  You Gotta Go  Raise your voice

00:22:30.810 --> 00:22:33.990
Sing!  Unleash your existence

00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:38.030
Get Away!  Until you surpass your limits

00:22:39.950 --> 00:22:41.950
Try It over and over

00:22:43.690 --> 00:22:50.110
In this world that spreads forever

00:22:50.460 --> 00:22:57.050
The timeline flows forever

00:22:57.340 --> 00:22:59.610
Nothing is certain

00:22:59.740 --> 00:23:01.290
In these isolated times

00:23:01.580 --> 00:23:03.020
Set Yourself Free without hesitation

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:04.790
Cuz We Still Believin' Magic

00:23:05.050 --> 00:23:08.220
The traces we leave behind

00:23:08.350 --> 00:23:11.790
The traces we leave behind

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:15.760
The miracles we create

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:17.970
Never Give Up Never!

00:23:17.970 --> 00:23:21.810
I won't give up  Never Give Up Never!

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:40.770
The ghostly Altergeists 
chase after their prey.

00:23:40.770 --> 00:23:46.870
Ghost Girl draws a beautiful path in 
the Data Storm and smiles in triumph.

00:23:47.120 --> 00:23:53.090
Playmaker looks for a tiny chance at victory.

00:23:53.090 --> 00:23:57.010
To turn this battle around, 
I have to bet on this.

00:23:57.010 --> 00:24:01.650
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:
Altergeist that Hides in the Darkness

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:04.010
Into the VRAINS!
